Fixes the broken connector rendering and adds per-segment styling.

## The bug

Connectors were drawn as one continuous dashed line spanning the whole series, behind the blocks. The dash pattern ran uninterrupted across all blocks, so each inter-block gap revealed a different arbitrary slice of the pattern — a stub here, nothing there (see the bug report screenshot).

## The fix

Every gap between adjacent blocks now gets its own line, center to center. Each line restarts the dash pattern at its block, so `dashed`/`dotted` render as uniform connectors in every gap. `solid` is visually unchanged.

## New API

```ts
connector: {
  color?: string;      // default: series block color
  thickness?: number;  // default: 2
  style?: 'solid' | 'dashed' | 'dotted'; // default: 'solid'
  segments?: Array<{
    span: [number, number]; // block indices at the two ends, inclusive
    color?: string;
    thickness?: number;
    style?: 'solid' | 'dashed' | 'dotted';
  }>;
}
```

- `span` is clamped to the rendered blocks; direction does not matter; zero-length spans are skipped.
- Long spans subdivide per gap so dash patterns stay uniform.
- When `segments` is present, only those render, in order (later entries draw over earlier ones); omitted fields fall back to the connector-level values.
- Backward compatible: `connector: { color, thickness, style }` (no `segments`) keeps its meaning — uniform styling across all gaps.

Example:

```ts
pictogram([6, 6], {
  connector: {
    thickness: 3,
    segments: [
      { span: [0, 2], color: '#f76e6e' },
      { span: [2, 5], color: '#52e081', style: 'dashed' },
    ],
  },
});
```

## Verification

- Core: 381/381 tests pass (connector suite rewritten for per-gap geometry + 8 new segment tests: per-segment colors, span subdivision, clamping/direction/zero-length, default inheritance + override, segments-replace-default, empty array, invalid segments)
- React: 82/82 pass (passthrough tests updated + new segments passthrough test)
- typecheck / lint / build clean; `pnpm size` passes all budgets
- Rendered the exact demo example from the bug report: 12 per-gap lines, each spanning exactly one pitch with its own dash pattern; segment colors verified in output SVG
- Bundle figures refreshed to latest measured: core barrel 12.18 kB, react barrel 12.07 kB, per-chart pictogram 3.06 kB
- Demo: new “Connector segments” example (multi-color spans); docs/API.md updated

Changeset: minor (`@samirdamle/nano-charts`).

